# Citation metadata for this repository.
#
# GitHub reads this file and renders a "Cite this repository" widget, and
# reference managers read it directly. CFF 1.2.0 schema:
# https://citation-file-format.github.io/
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Two saturating operators: non-substitutability of human and machine contribution in AI-assisted discovery"
abstract: >-
  Humans and AI systems are usually placed on one capability curve and asked who
  is ahead. That framing has no formal content. We formalize the alternative:
  the two parties act on different variables, and each saturates on a different
  axis. A machine, holding the hypothesis space fixed, compresses the residual
  toward a floor it cannot pass, with total gain bounded by log(e0/Phi) and no
  improvement from more inference steps. A human, holding the hypothesis space
  fixed, moves the floor itself, and the gain is unbounded. Two further
  saturations fall out of the same currency: headcount saturates immediately
  because a max-type coalition's marginal member earns exactly zero, and corpus
  size saturates because only the single item certifying the lowest floor
  determines the attainable bound. We formalize all of this in Lean 4: 153
  machine-checked theorems and 20 worked examples across twelve modules, with
  zero sorry and no axioms beyond Classical.choice, Quot.sound and propext.
type: article
